## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle): **248 C fiber-IR
overlap under a zone-mean model**.

- Trigger: weekend splice leaves 0.4 pct already-open residual; 16 min
  of hold writes 18 pct overlap and 248 C fiber IR; zone mean stays 218 C.
- Base rate: <1% — 0.34%/hold from a creel-traverse MC (flyer-gap spec
  designed; overlap fitted-style).
- Naive failure: FALSE PERMISSION. PB-CF-11 sees ZMEAN 218 C, TENS
  22 N, O2 19.4, raises, ships an overlapped creel, $4.18M.
- Trajectory edit: put the overlap in `state.fault_context`, make the
  zone-mean model the mechanism that keeps all three confirms green,
  and force the gate to refuse the raise on r_hot 248 even though all
  three playbook confirms are numerically true.

Distinct from the domain injection: the domain is the PAN oxidation oven;
the tail is the accidental model-nullspace compound.

## Neuromorphic Translator

Race window [6.746, 7.246] ms = 500 us. Winner hot.ir @ 6.818 ms
(amplitude 1.26, 248 C). Loser zmean.ok @ 7.010 ms (amplitude
1.09, 218 C). Margin 192 us vs combined jitter 62 us (3.10x).
overlap.cam @ 7.154 ms is a third race-window channel. Gate @ 7.518 ms
= winner + 700 us.

Flip narrative: 192 us < min(500, 500) us, so order is flip-fragile. If
zmean-ok wins, PB-CF-11 heads the triage queue. The hold must ride
order-invariant floors (r_hot, r_overlap), not the winner tag.

